Z||000000||ChadMan||10-07-1999||05:25 PM||||So there I was, coming home from work and merging into traffic in the 88 Coupe.  I see a nice big hole to merge into in front of a fairly-new Chevy Astro and a solid wall of traffic behind him.  <P>I'm going about 60, and he's going about 60, so I downshift to 4th and floor it, and wouldn't you know, this guy floors it too - and he's faster!  I ease up, and he eases up in an attempt to keep me from merging.  So I floor it again, and when he does too, I nail the brakes, cut hard left, go clear to the center lane and floor it again, taking a full carlength-lead while he tries to figure out where I went.  <P>When he sees me blast by on the left, he floors it again, and pulls alongside, despite the fact that I'm now doing more than 80 mph.  But he can't pull ahead before we hit more traffic, and he's forced to ease off, after which he resumes his 60 mph cruising speed - which makes me wonder why in the hell he didn't just let me merge in the first place.<P>Had I been driving the V6, there'd have been no contest whatsoever.  Still, for an Astro to whip even a 4-banger Fiero, he had to be packing the 4.3 Vortec.  I think I'll go re-read the "4.3 Vortec Swap" thread...||||reg||1
Z||000001||RFMike||10-07-1999||08:03 PM||||There was a post on about horns elsewhere.  The air horns for the guy in the Astro should scream, "You're a 4 wheel ******* ."  <BR>Sorry, but you found one of my hot buttons.  Dorks like that shouldn't be allowed to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-08-1999||02:42 AM||||I know what you mean RFMike, about 15 years ago, an *******  like that almost got me killed with a stunt like that. I was driving a Chrysler 1308 at that time and I was driving behind another car that was doing about 30mph where the speedlimit was 50mph. I checked the left lane for on-coming traffic and there was only a truck in the far distance so I changed lanes to pass him. The second that guy saw I was next to him, he accelerated, making it impossible for me to pass. When I slowed down to get back in my lane he slowed down too. Whatever I tried, the guy wouldn't let me back in the right lane again. In the end I had to stear my car off the road on the left, avoiding a head-on collision with the truck. Scariest moment I ever had in a car.||||reg||1
