Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||10-08-1999||05:04 AM||||Shiner, unfortunately stunts like this cause quite a few traffic deaths here in Holland. The traffic here is incredibly aggresive, compared to the States for instance. In the States there are some situations that we could <B>never</B> have, for instance 4-way stop signs. If you would have that here in Holland, you would constantly have 4-way collisions!<P>Aggresive behavior in traffic is a real problem here - partly because of the tremendous amounts of cars on the road: around 7-8 million cars on 15 million people!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||10-08-1999||12:54 PM||||I think that with the proliferation of guns and easy to obtain concealed weapons permits in the US, much of this type of driving activity is discouraged.  It is not that rare for a case of "road rage" to result in the offending driver being shot at, or even killed.  I have found that in the larger cities where this type of thing has recently occured, the drivers are very curteous for quite some time afterwards.  Note:  I do not advocate shooting someone because of their lack of proper driving attitude.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||10-08-1999||01:10 PM||||Sometimes I think some cars should come with James Bond-style missile launchers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I live in a small town, so luckily I don't see too much of that kind of driving. However, it seems that the majority of the people in my town don't understand the concept of a "stop sign".. I came to that conclusion after I saw a police car run a stop sign.. he slowed down, but didn't stop. wasn't chasing anyone either, just driving around. Not nearly as bad as one time when an old lady ran a red light and then proceeded to speed past a school bus that was letting kids off...<P>Speaking of Chevy Astros, a friend of mine used to drive one (his parents.) and I recall it being pretty fast. Couple of times we almost got killed.. it was stupid, yes.. but pretty fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>(ever pulled a corner at 150kph in a minivan??)||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||10-08-1999||09:53 PM||||A few years ago came home from College for a few days...     Hey, mom got a new Windstar, lets see how I like it.  Got out on 725, (larger 4 lane divided road in Centerville) Went to go from a light, couldn't figure out who was squealling their tires until I looked in the mirror and nocticed I smoked the tires (big time) on my mom's new ride(pure accident, my sable didn't compare).  She still doesn't know and I plan to keep it that way.  That minivan with its 3.8 is very quick.  I don't like to drive it, because I'm used to giving my car the gas, do it in the minivan, and all the neigbors look at you.||||reg||11
