Z||000017||Cooter||10-09-1999||06:08 PM||||My other car has hood mounted windshield washer sprayers. I found that the spray can be adjusted by sticking a pin in the nozzle and moving to the desired location. In my case, I aimed one of the driver's side nozzles to spray to the side of the car. One hit the windshield, the other hit those rude fast food workers in the drive through windows! There is just something about watching hot washer fluid hit someone in the back that really makes me laugh.||||reg||14
Z||000018||fiero56||10-09-1999||07:23 PM||||I have a friend who does that.  He has a mazda, and when he has a tailgater he loves to just hit the washer button.  His spray way over the roof of his car though, very high pressure, I think they're misaligned. I made the mistake of following him home once, and when I high-beamed him, just to tick him off, he hit those jets! I didn't know what hit me. All of a sudden it pouring rain on me, then I realized it was his washers.  You should see him hit those convertibles, they go another route. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
